    "RIGHT_TO_LEFT": 4
  },
  "affine_negativity_semantics": "The affine reduction sigma2_tau = q*dt*(tau + c_direction) is EXACT only for tau >= 8 and is FORBIDDEN below tau = 8. Where it is (wrongly) evaluated below tau = 8 it returns a strictly NEGATIVE variance for every integer tau in [1, affine_last_negative_tau] and a strictly POSITIVE variance for every integer tau >= affine_first_positive_tau, per direction. The boundary is direction-specific because c_LTR = -4.355500526064508 and c_RTL = -3.395856222446993, so the sign change lies at tau = -c_direction: 4.3555 for LEFT_TO_RIGHT and 3.3959 for RIGHT_TO_LEFT. There is no integer tau at which the affine form is exactly zero.",
